          "start_ms": null,
          "status": "needs-review",
          "text": "Description: On February 7, 2013, around 9:45 PM, a witness and his wife observed the slow movement of an object that intrigued them. The witness's description has all the characteristics of an aircraft on final approach: a slow-moving bright shape, then a black cylindrical shape. The time he mentions, 9:45 PM, coincides with the arrival of Air Corsica Flight Marseille-Bastia, which departs Marseille at 9:05 PM and is expected to land in Bastia at 9:55 PM; this could correspond to what he observed. The Bastia Poretta Airport is located 3 or 4 kilometers as the crow flies from the observation location, to the northwest. See the attached approach trajectories for the Bastia airport: in red is the path used with a southwesterly wind, as was the case that day (see weather report). What is surprising is the witness's surprise, who states the phenomenon was two times lower than usual aircraft; note that the witness was not at his home, giving him a different perspective from his usual viewpoint. It is also possible that the pilot used a lower approach altitude that day for reasons specific to him. The GEIPAN classifies this case as \"A\": observation of the Marseille-Bastia flight on final approach for landing.",
          "translation_text_sha256": "87d59b853966493aa618cad2144fef704e2e0dfaebc585ff42e68e6efeb82789"
        }
      ],
